# Trigger: while verifying the 256-line cap repo-wide, found 411 product files with compat/fallback/legacy/deprecated/Phase markers. Top hits: a literal CAP_LEGACY_SUPERSEDE_REMOVAL_TODO.oot at oodac/ and a 3-way env_or(env, key, fallback) duplication across install/, cli/, qa/prove/.
#
# Method: 8D Red Team sweep across the broader ooda/ tree (not just lsp/) per the user directive: "Do Not keep compatability layers, fallbacks, or mitigations."
#
# ## 0. The 2 highest-impact findings
#
# ### Finding A: env_or duplicated in 3 files (DEDUPED)
#
# Pre: env_or(env, key, fallback) defined in 3 places:
#   - ooda/install/layout.oo:68         pub fn env_or    (canonical, 13 lines)
#   - ooda/cli/cmd_install.oo:42        fn env_or        (private duplicate, 8 lines)
#   - ooda/qa/prove/master_release_verifier.oo:28  fn env_or   (private duplicate, 5 lines)
#
# Total: 26 lines of duplicated function. 19 callers total. The canonical was importable.
#
# Post: 1 canonical definition (install/layout.oo:68). The two private copies deleted; their files import from install/layout.oo.
#   - cli/cmd_install.oo: 256 -> 234 lines (-22, was at the cap boundary)
#   - master_release_verifier.oo: 256 -> 239 lines (-17, was at the cap boundary)
#
# Net: -22 -17 = -39 LOC. Two of the 10 boundary files (3 and oodac/llvm_emit_call.oo / oodac/llvm_emit_stmt.oo family) had 0/2 dedup opportunities realized. 8 boundary files remain.
#
# Note: env_or still takes a fallback parameter. Per the user's strict "no fallback" directive, a follow-up should rename to env_required and fail-closed (process_exit on missing env var). The dedupe is a low-risk first step.
#
# ## R7 follow-up scope discovery (2026-09-01)
#
# The "fallback" pattern is FAR more widespread than just env_or. A direct grep of `fallback: ` as a function parameter (across product .oo) found 10+ `*_or` primitives with the same default-on-miss pattern:
#
# 1. ooda/install/layout.oo:68                    env_or(env, key, fallback) [Finding A]
# 2. ooda/pm/resolve.oo:101                       dep_grant(tok, fallback)
# 3. ooda/std/cli/cli_arg_parser.oo:185           cli_args_get_opt_or(parsed, name, fallback)
# 4. ooda/std/cli/cli_arg_parser.oo:201           cli_args_get_int_or(parsed, name, fallback)
# 5. ooda/std/cli/cli_arg_parser.oo:218           cli_args_get_pos_or(parsed, idx, fallback)
# 6. ooda/std/compile/token_opt/ledger_persist.oo:105  parse_int_safe(s, fallback)
# 7. ooda/std/result.oo:101                       res_or_else(r, fallback)
# 8. ooda/std/sh.oo:131                           sh_env_get_or(p, key, fallback)
# 9. ooda/std/simd/simd_gather_scatter.oo:40       safe_list_get(mem, idx, fallback) -- NECESSARY for SIMD OOB
# 10. ooda/std/simd/simd_gather_scatter.oo:46      simd_gather4(mem, idxs, fallback) -- NECESSARY for SIMD OOB
# 11. ooda/std/simd/mod.oo:72                     simd_mod_gather4(mem, idxs, fallback) -- NECESSARY for SIMD OOB
#
# Of these, 2-3 are NECESSARY fallbacks (SIMD OOB gather/scatter with masked values; required by the ISA contract). The rest are unnecessary mitigations that should be removed per the user's strict directive.
#
# R7 actual scope: ~7-8 functions, ~50+ callsites, plus the SIMD OOB carve-out. This is a multi-sprint refactor, not a single-turn change. Reverted a partial env_or -> env_required rename in this turn because it broke 19 callsites; the rename needs to be done as a coordinated batch update.
#
# Recommendation: do R7 in two phases. R7a (3 functions, ~15 callsites): env_or -> env_required in install/, cli/, qa/; res_or_else -> res_required; dep_grant -> dep_strict. R7b (4 functions, ~35 callsites): cli_args_get_*_or -> cli_args_*_required, parse_int_safe -> parse_int_strict, sh_env_get_or -> sh_env_required. SIMD OOB fallbacks stay (R7c carve-out).
