# ### Finding B: CAP_LEGACY_SUPERSEDE_REMOVAL_TODO.oot (R6 EXECUTION COMPLETE 2026-09-01)
#
# File: ooda/oodac/CAP_LEGACY_SUPERSEDE_REMOVAL_TODO.oot (84 lines).
# Content: documents that after "Issue 2 of the red-team fix", the cap_*_granted_ok and cap_*_argflow_ok helpers in oodac/check_cap_grant.oo no longer accept the broad NetCap / FsCap / SysCap / AllocCap as a supersede for the granular preferred kind. Callers must declare the granular cap they actually need.
# Migration rules table: 8 sealed-op categories x broad cap -> granular cap replacement.
#
# CORRECTION CHAIN (3 successive turns of negative-trust):
# 1. CAP_LEGACY TODO claimed 52 callers. Direct grep returned 11 files (2 enforcers that correctly keep broad caps to reject them, leaving 9 real).
# 2. Of the 9, ZERO have broad caps in actual function signatures. All references are in string literals (error messages, fix hints, comments).
# 3. Of the 9, 2 are canonical cap-recognition lists (ast_emit_outline.oo, ast_emit_reflect.oo) — those are NOT doc-drift, they're feature-correct.
#
# Final R6 scope: 7 doc-drift files. Status: ALL FIXED this turn.
#
# ## R6 execution record (8 files modified, 0 lines added)
#
# 1. c_emit_lower.oo (5 doc-drift strings fixed):
#    - read_file/path_exists/file_size: &FsCap -> &FsReadCap (lines 133, 146, 152)
#    - write_file: &FsCap -> &FsWriteCap (line 140)
#    - sys_exec: &ProcessCap or &SysCap -> &ProcessCap only (line 164) (sys_exec per migration table is &ProcessCap)
#    - fetch: &NetCap -> &HttpCap (line 176) (fetch per migration table is &HttpCap)
#    - alloc_bytes/malloc/free_bytes/free/realloc: stay &AllocCap (correct per migration table: &AllocCap is reserved for these ops)
# 2. c_emit_sys.oo (3 doc-drift strings fixed):
#    - sys_spawn/sys_wait/sys_kill: &SysCap -> &ProcessCap (per migration table: process ops)
#    - 9 other &SysCap refs stay (sys_epoll_create, sys_inotify_init, sys_prctl, landlock_restrict, oo_rlimit_set_*, oo_cap_kernel_seal, oo_enclave_enter — all residual OS ops per migration table)
# 3. c_emit_netio.oo (9 doc-drift strings fixed):
#    - tcp_bind: &NetCap -> &BindCap
#    - tcp_connect/tcp_read/tcp_write/tcp_close/tls_connect: &NetCap -> &TcpCap
#    - bind_udp/udp_recv/udp_send: &NetCap -> &UdpCap
#    - sock_raw stays &NetCap (correct per migration table: &NetCap reserved exclusively for sock_raw/raw_socket)
# 4. x86_emit_cap.oo (2 doc-drift strings fixed):
#    - Comment line 8: "Scan for capability tokens &SysCap, &FsCap, &AllocCap, &ThreadCap" -> "&SysCap (residual OS), &FsReadCap, &FsWriteCap, &AllocCap, &ThreadCap"
#    - Error msg line 32: "ambient I/O requires &SysCap, &FsCap, &AllocCap, or &ThreadCap" -> "ambient I/O requires &SysCap (residual), &FsReadCap/&FsWriteCap, &AllocCap, or &ThreadCap"
# 5. x86_emit_elf.oo (1 doc-drift comment fixed):
#    - Line 5: "The pure path takes &FsCap" -> "The pure path takes &FsWriteCap" (function actually takes &FsWriteCap)
# 6. load_import.oo (1 doc-drift comment fixed):
#    - Line 5: "Callers pass &FsCap and a path" -> "Callers pass &FsReadCap and a path" (functions actually take &FsReadCap)
# 7. diag_json.oo (2 doc-drift fix hints updated):
#    - Line 60: "Add matching &FsCap/&SysCap/&EnvCap/&NetCap/..." -> "Add matching &FsReadCap/&FsWriteCap (per op), &EnvCap, &HttpCap/&TcpCap/&UdpCap/&BindCap/&NetCap(sock_raw), &TimeCap, &RandCap, &AllocCap, or &UnsafeFFICap"
#    - Line 124: "Add capability handle parameter &NetCap/&FsCap/&SysCap" -> "Add capability handle parameter (per op: &HttpCap, &TcpCap, &UdpCap, &BindCap, &NetCap(sock_raw), &FsReadCap, &FsWriteCap, &ProcessCap, &SysCap(residual))"
#
